  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For the system of linear equations:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math></p><p>Consider the following statements:<br />(A) The system has unique solution if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math><br />(B) The system has unique solution if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math><br />(C) The system has unique solution if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math><br />(D) The system has no-solution if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math><br />(E) The system has infinite number of solutions if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>&#8800;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;</p><p>Which of the following statements are correct?</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
